Ask the kernel for the thread ID on Linux.

The server signals threads with tgkill, so it needs the kernel's ID.
pthread_getthreadid_np returns that on FreeBSD, but llvm-libc also has the
function and returns the ID libc++ uses for std::thread, which is not the
kernel's.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -1529,10 +1529,10 @@
 static int get_unix_tid(void)
 {
     int ret = -1;
-#ifdef HAVE_PTHREAD_GETTHREADID_NP
-    ret = pthread_getthreadid_np();
-#elif defined(linux)
+#if defined(linux)
     ret = syscall( __NR_gettid );
+#elif defined(HAVE_PTHREAD_GETTHREADID_NP)
+    ret = pthread_getthreadid_np();
 #elif defined(__sun)
     ret = pthread_self();
 #elif defined(__APPLE__)
